  "body": "<rss version=\"2.0\"><channel><title>Public audit fixture</title><item>\n\t\t<title>Researchers Are Using Meta’s Open-Weight AI Models to Transform Medicine</title>\n\t\t<link>https://about.fb.com/news/2026/11/researchers-using-meta-open-weight-ai-models-medical-breakthroughs/</link>\n\t\t\n\t\t<dc:creator><![CDATA[Facebook]]></dc:creator>\n\t\t<pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:00:01 +0000</pubDate>\n\t\t\t\t<category><![CDATA[Meta]]></category>\n\t\t<category><![CDATA[Meta Quest]]></category>\n\t\t<category><![CDATA[Recent News]]></category>\n\t\t<category><![CDATA[Sidebar - Featured]]></category>\n\t\t<category><![CDATA[Technology and Innovation]]></category>\n\t\t<category><![CDATA[AI]]></category>\n\t\t<category><![CDATA[Mixed Reality]]></category>\n\t\t<category><![CDATA[Open Source]]></category>\n\t\t<guid isPermaLink=\"false\">https://about.fb.com/?p=50883</guid>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t<description><![CDATA[<div><img width=\"890\" height=\"501\" src=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Thumbnail-1.jpg?fit=890%2C501\" class=\"attachment-large size-large wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 15px;\" srcset=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Thumbnail-1.jpg?w=1920 1920w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Thumbnail-1.jpg?w=300 300w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Thumbnail-1.jpg?w=768 768w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Thumbnail-1.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Thumbnail-1.jpg?w=1536 1536w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Thumbnail-1.jpg?w=800 800w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Thumbnail-1.jpg?w=1780 1780w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 890px) 100vw, 890px\" /></div>\n<p>We brought researchers together for the Open Source AI For Science Summit, where they shared how they’re using AI to accelerate scientific discovery. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://about.fb.com/news/2026/11/researchers-using-meta-open-weight-ai-models-medical-breakthroughs/\">Researchers Are Using Meta’s Open-Weight AI Models to Transform Medicine</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://about.fb.com\">Meta Newsroom</a>.</p>\n]]></description>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<content:encoded><![CDATA[<div><img width=\"890\" height=\"501\" src=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Thumbnail-1.jpg?fit=890%2C501\" class=\"attachment-large size-large wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 15px;\" srcset=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Thumbnail-1.jpg?w=1920 1920w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Thumbnail-1.jpg?w=300 300w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Thumbnail-1.jpg?w=768 768w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Thumbnail-1.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Thumbnail-1.jpg?w=1536 1536w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Thumbnail-1.jpg?w=800 800w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Thumbnail-1.jpg?w=1780 1780w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 890px) 100vw, 890px\" /></div><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Open science is critical to advancing medical research. To accelerate this progress, we’ve expanded our </span><a href=\"https://about.fb.com/news/2026/10/meta-partners-with-five-us-universities-to-accelerate-medical-and-scientific-breakthroughs/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">academic partnerships</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, giving researchers funding and access to our AI models like Muse Glimmer, SAM3, DINOv3, and Brain2Qwertyv2. These researchers are </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">independently adapting our models for their own investigational research. </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Here are a few of the projects that are benefitting from our partnership: </span></p>\n<h2>Training Doctors in Virtual Reality</h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At Louisiana State University, Dr. Peter DeBlieux and his team are using Muse Glimmer, SAM 3, DINOv3, and other models from Meta, along with Meta Quest 3 headsets to develop COPES, an experimental coaching platform that supports healthcare professionals with medical procedural training in virtual reality. The system will aim to provide adaptive guidance, real-time performance assessment, and personalized feedback across technical execution, patient communication, clinical reasoning, and decision-making. Working virtually means medical students can learn complicated procedures in situations where practicing on real patients may be risky, and virtual instruction means more medical professionals can receive high quality technical and communications training — no matter where they are. </span></p>\n<div class=\"fbcorp-inline-audio-card\"><div class=\"fbcorp-inline-audio-image\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"960\" height=\"344\" src=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Peter-2.jpg?fit=960%2C344&#038;resize=960%2C344\" class=\"fbcorp-inline-audio-artwork wp-image-51049\" alt=\"Photo of Peter DeBlieux, MD, LSU Health New Orleans School of Medicine\" srcset=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Peter-2.jpg?w=3309 3309w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Peter-2.jpg?w=300 300w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Peter-2.jpg?w=768 768w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Peter-2.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Peter-2.jpg?w=1536 1536w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Peter-2.jpg?w=2048 2048w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Peter-2.jpg?w=1920 1920w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Peter-2.jpg?w=800 800w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Peter-2.jpg?w=2880 2880w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\" /></div><div class=\"wp-block-audio\"><audio data-fbcorp-inline-audio-title=\"Meta’s Quest 3 Headsets and Open Weight AI Models Are Improving Doctor Training\" class=\"wp-audio-shortcode\" id=\"audio-50883-1\" preload=\"none\" style=\"width: 100%;\" controls=\"controls\"><source type=\"audio/wav\" src=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/NRP_NEWS-3325__PeterDeBlieux_v2.wav?_=1\" /><a href=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/NRP_NEWS-3325__PeterDeBlieux_v2.wav\">https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/NRP_NEWS-3325__PeterDeBlieux_v2.wav</a></audio></div></div>\n<h2>Helping Doctors Find the Source of Epilepsy</h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Dr. Pierre Bourdillon at Rothschild Hospital Foundation is using AI research and models from Meta including </span><a href=\"https://facebookresearch.github.io/neuroai/neuralset/index.html\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">NeuralSet</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, </span><a href=\"https://facebookresearch.github.io/brain2qwerty/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Brain2Qwertyv2</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, </span><a href=\"https://aidemos.atmeta.com/tribev2\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Tribev2</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, and </span><a href=\"https://ai.meta.com/research/dinov3/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">DINOv3</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, in research projects aimed at better understanding the source of epilepsy in the brain. Currently, epilepsy can’t be directly visualized in brain images, making it difficult for clinicians to identify its source. Dr. Bourdillon is using AI to develop a tool that can enable simulations of epileptic seizures originating in different regions of the brain. This approach could one day enable doctors to select the simulation that best matches their patient’s case, allowing them to form a strong hypothesis about where the patient’s epilepsy originates. This early-stage research could improve accuracy in a range of epilepsy treatments, including surgical removal of affected brain tissue and device implantation designed to disrupt epileptic activity. The simulations also have the potential to help researchers address speech and motor restoration in patients with brain injuries.</span></p>\n<div class=\"fbcorp-inline-audio-card\"><div class=\"fbcorp-inline-audio-image\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"960\" height=\"344\" src=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Pierre-2.jpg?fit=960%2C344&#038;resize=960%2C344\" class=\"fbcorp-inline-audio-artwork wp-image-51050\" alt=\"Photo of Pierre Bourdillon, MD, PhhD, Head of TITAN Laboratory, Paris Cite University\" srcset=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Pierre-2.jpg?w=3309 3309w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Pierre-2.jpg?w=300 300w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Pierre-2.jpg?w=768 768w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Pierre-2.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Pierre-2.jpg?w=1536 1536w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Pierre-2.jpg?w=2048 2048w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Pierre-2.jpg?w=1920 1920w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Pierre-2.jpg?w=800 800w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Pierre-2.jpg?w=2880 2880w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\" /></div><div class=\"wp-block-audio\"><audio data-fbcorp-inline-audio-title=\"How Researchers Are Using Meta’s AI Models to Predict the Source of Epilepsy in the Brain\" class=\"wp-audio-shortcode\" id=\"audio-50883-2\" preload=\"none\" style=\"width: 100%;\" controls=\"controls\"><source type=\"audio/wav\" src=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/NRP_NEWS-3325__PierreBourdillon_v4.wav?_=2\" /><a href=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/NRP_NEWS-3325__PierreBourdillon_v4.wav\">https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/NRP_NEWS-3325__PierreBourdillon_v4.wav</a></audio></div></div>\n<h2>Improving Our Understanding of Rare Diseases</h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At Columbia University, Dr. Wolfgang Pernice has partnered with Meta to adapt the DINO family of models to improve analysis of microscopy images of cells, helping doctors understand how rare diseases appear in cells. In conventional image analysis methods, researchers have to know what they are looking for in advance, limiting their analysis. But the adapted Cell-DINO, DINO-BoC, and FINO models generate unbiased representations of the inner workings of cells, allowing scientists to decode the complex patterns by which rare diseases manifest in human cells. This can help improve our understanding of rare diseases and accelerate drug discovery. </span></p>\n<div class=\"fbcorp-inline-audio-card\"><div class=\"fbcorp-inline-audio-image\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"960\" height=\"344\" src=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Wolfgang-1.jpg?fit=960%2C344&#038;resize=960%2C344\" class=\"fbcorp-inline-audio-artwork wp-image-50984\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Wolfgang-1.jpg?w=3309 3309w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Wolfgang-1.jpg?w=300 300w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Wolfgang-1.jpg?w=768 768w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Wolfgang-1.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Wolfgang-1.jpg?w=1536 1536w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Wolfgang-1.jpg?w=2048 2048w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Wolfgang-1.jpg?w=1920 1920w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Wolfgang-1.jpg?w=800 800w, https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Wolfgang-1.jpg?w=2880 2880w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\" /></div><div class=\"wp-block-audio\"><audio data-fbcorp-inline-audio-title=\"Understanding How Rare Diseases Appear in Cells Using Meta’s Open Weight AI Models\" class=\"wp-audio-shortcode\" id=\"audio-50883-3\" preload=\"none\" style=\"width: 100%;\" controls=\"controls\"><source type=\"audio/wav\" src=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/NRP_NEWS-3325__WolfgangPernice_v2.wav?_=3\" /><a href=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/NRP_NEWS-3325__WolfgangPernice_v2.wav\">https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/NRP_NEWS-3325__WolfgangPernice_v2.wav</a></audio></div></div>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Each of these investigational projects highlights AI’s unique ability to fill critical research gaps.  While all of the work featured here is early-stage, we look forward to the potential breakthroughs enabled by our AI models. To learn more about our Open Source AI for Science Summit, where we interviewed the researchers, head to </span><a href=\"http://research.meta.ai/blog/ai-for-science-summit\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">our AI blog</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://about.fb.com/news/2026/11/researchers-using-meta-open-weight-ai-models-medical-breakthroughs/\">Researchers Are Using Meta’s Open-Weight AI Models to Transform Medicine</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://about.fb.com\">Meta Newsroom</a>.</p>\n]]></content:encoded>\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t<post-id xmlns=\"com-wordpress:feed-additions:1\">50883</post-id><thumbnail>https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Thumbnail-1.jpg?fit=890%2C501</thumbnail>\n\t\t<media:thumbnail url=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Header-1.jpg?fit=3840%2C2160\" />\n\t\t<media:content url=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/Researchers-Are-Using-Metas-Open-Weight-AI-Models-to-Transform-Medicine_Header-1.jpg?fit=3840%2C2160\" medium=\"image\">\n\t\t\t<media:title type=\"html\">Researchers Are Using Meta’s Open Weight AI Models to Transform Medicine_Header (1)</media:title>\n\t\t</media:content>\n\n\t\t<media:content url=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/NRP_NEWS-3325__PeterDeBlieux_v2.wav\" medium=\"audio\" />\n\n\t\t<media:content url=\"https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2027/11/NRP_NEWS-3325__PierreBourdillon_v4.wav\" medium=\"audio\" />\n\t</item></channel></rss>"
